{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"LANDED. Gerrit 1940 MERGED (rebased server-side to `b91f8f6830` on origin/main). Gates: LLM-Review +1 (rebar review bot), Verified +1 (rebar CI bot), 0 unresolved comments. CI run 32325093416 all green — lint+type-check, pytest on ubuntu py3.11/3.12/3.13 and macos py3.13, golden-path clean install, optionality/lean-runtime, artifact provenance, pip-audit, eval-discipline, mutation shard selection, whole-store authorship gate.\n\nPost-merge sizes on main: `_config_sources.py` 403 LOC, `_config_resolvers.py` 480 LOC.\n\nOne ADVISORY (non-blocking) code-review finding, recorded here rather than churned into a patchset: `test_config_resolvers_is_a_recognised_composition_root` asserts the gate's internal constant `COMPOSITION_ROOT_BASENAMES` instead of the gate's observable classification behaviour, so it would break on a behaviour-preserving refactor of that gate. The stronger form is the one `tests/scripts/test_check_config_ownership_heldout.py` already uses — build a synthetic tree with an env read in a file named `_config_resolvers.py` and assert `gate.check(root) == []`. Worth folding into the next change that touches either file; not worth a fresh patchset and full CI cycle on its own, since the seam membership it guards is independently enforced by `scripts/check_config_ownership.py` running in `make lint` on every commit."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787195223069214001,"uuid":"e7e0f253-1277-4029-936b-4acfd5e1706d"}